"Join table names are STRICT: a table joining apples and oranges is named apples_oranges; additional relation semantics append at the END (apples_oranges_progressions, apples_oranges_territories), which also resolves collisions when several distinct relations exist between the same two tables. NAME ORDER: the OWNER of the relation comes first; when ownership is unclear, the more important entity (usually the more used throughout the code) comes first. Never bury one side of a join (a 'quest_progress' hiding its entity side violates this -- it is entities_quests_progress: the entity owns its progress)."